WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.933
- Hey guys, it's Justine.

00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:03.230
And today we're testing
out the new iPhone 12 Pro.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.930
I'm gonna take some photos
and videos but first,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.860
thank you to dbrand for
sponsoring this video

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.560
because I just put on
their new tempered glass

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.370
screen protector and this thing is...

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.810
It just blew my mind.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.510
New iPhones mean new dbrand skins.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.140
We also have one of their cases

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.260
but we also have something new,

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.010
we have their new tempered
glass screen protector.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.550
And why this is very exciting
is because the new iPhone 12

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.380
is a completely flat display.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.670
It will allow for some
very precise placement

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.070
of the screen protectors.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:32.907
You might be saying Justine

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:35.840
'Yeah, but the new iPhone
12 has new Ceramic Shield

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.990
which is four times stronger
than the previous iPhone 11.'

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.200
Yes, it is but it is about the same

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.620
as far as scratch resistance,

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.750
so I do not wanna make the
same mistake I did last year

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.610
by not putting a screen protector on mine.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:49.660
So we're starting off
this iPhone 12 right.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.587
I mean they even give you a
little screen bubble pusher.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.170
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.512 --> 00:01:05.929
(upbeat music continues)

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.640
- Wow!

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.793
This is perfect.

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:17.690
(knife scratching)

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.590
- Oh my God, it's not
even scratching it at all.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.210
I just thought okay I'll stab it

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.330
and if it does scratch it,

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.163
cool, great,

00:01:24.163 --> 00:01:25.010
I have another one.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.393
I'll put that one on.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.405
I'm so impressed. Let's
get a case on this thing.

00:01:31.405 --> 00:01:33.988
(upbeat music)

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.740
- Oh, hear that!

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.440
That looks good.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.003
Oh, did you need to dbrand your MagSafe?

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:47.250
You could do that too.

00:01:50.348 --> 00:01:51.470
That's great.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:54.810
Okay, back or not, oh it's a little windy.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.020
Back on Life on Tyler's here.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:56.880
Hi Tyler.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:57.713
And like I've said before,

00:01:57.713 --> 00:02:00.500
the biggest difference
between the 12 and the 12 Pro

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.590
is the 12 does not have a telephoto lens

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:04.600
and you could only shoot in 30 fps

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.240
as opposed to the 60
frames Dolby Vision HDR.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.260
So, let's go take some
photos and videos, yes?

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:14.260
I still got a sprained ankle
so we'll take this real slow.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:15.920
It is so beautiful.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.890
It just rained so it feels so fresh,

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.240
it's so fresh.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.857
What is that? Is that a
person or is that a...

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.887
That is a person's
feet, are they flipping?

00:02:26.887 --> 00:02:30.103
Yes, they're doing some sort of activity.

00:02:31.082 --> 00:02:33.665
(upbeat music)

00:02:43.421 --> 00:02:46.838
(upbeat music continues)

00:02:52.741 --> 00:02:54.400
- Should we take a
picture of these people?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.700
One thing I wouldn't be able to do

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.750
if I was shooting this on the
12 is there's no telephoto,

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.433
but we'll be able to see them.

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:04.131
(upbeat music)

00:03:16.648 --> 00:03:20.065
(upbeat music continues)

00:03:31.148 --> 00:03:34.565
(upbeat music continues)

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:45.470
- I'm using the OSMO Mobile 4

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.340
to stabilize my shot as I'm walking.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.010
It already has really
incredible stabilization

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.320
but just having this added
gimbal to get these shots

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.760
makes it look so much cooler.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.490
One thing that I am excited
to show you guys though

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:57.210
is the difference between HDR footage

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.830
on the 12 Pro and the 11,

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.940
because right now you're not
actually able to see the HDR

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.620
because I'm exporting this video on STR.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.000
But when you are really
taking this into final cut,

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.660
you're able to see the color detail,

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.950
you're able to see how
much more color you...

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.083
It's windy again!

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.110
They just asked who I was talking to.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.200
I'm talking to my friends on YouTube.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.670
So because I'm posting this
on YouTube it is an STR clip

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.240
You're not gonna really be
able to see the difference

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.880
but when you do take this into final cut

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.770
and comparing the footage
between the 12 and the 11,

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:26.900
there is such a huge difference

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.690
because you have so
much more color detail,

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:31.200
you have the ability to bring
up and down the highlights

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.300
so much more than you could
in the non-HDR footage.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.490
So a lot of you guys keep saying

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.800
'but it looks the same'

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.100
I promise you, as someone
who has edited this video

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.356
and other ones, it is not the same.

00:04:42.356 --> 00:04:44.939
(upbeat music)

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.470
- The front-facing camera's also amazing

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.350
because they have added an update to this

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.960
so you'll be able to do
front-facing Night Mode

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:01.793
which is kinda cool.

00:05:01.793 --> 00:05:02.950
I haven't really got to test it out

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.000
as much as I'd like.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.930
I did a little bit but
sometimes when it's really dark,

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:10.145
I just use the flash to get a good selfie

00:05:10.145 --> 00:05:12.060
but the fact that they've added Night Mode

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.830
on all of these lenses is pretty cool.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.012
Speechless.

00:05:16.012 --> 00:05:17.117
(waves rolling)

00:05:17.117 --> 00:05:20.400
- It just takes a good
photo every single time

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.423
That's a nice photo.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.053
That's a nice photo.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.116
That's wasn't a nice photo.

00:05:28.116 --> 00:05:30.699
(upbeat music)

00:05:40.986 --> 00:05:44.403
(upbeat music continues)

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:57.607
(upbeat music continues)

00:06:08.473 --> 00:06:10.223
- [Justine] Hey bird!

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.793
(upbeat music)

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.360
- Everything in Ultra Wide
just looks terrifying.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.730
This looks like I'm at the
Grand Canyon right now.

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:29.740
I'm not.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:30.573
Spoiler!

00:06:31.426 --> 00:06:34.009
(upbeat music)

00:06:47.648 --> 00:06:51.065
(upbeat music continues)

00:07:04.475 --> 00:07:06.808
- Let's get that wide angle.

00:07:07.956 --> 00:07:11.717
I found a rock, it's pretty.

00:07:13.189 --> 00:07:15.606
(soft music)

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.530
- It's nighttime which
means it's Night Mode time.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.782
Night Mode is available
on every single camera

00:07:38.782 --> 00:07:40.290
on the iPhone 12,

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:43.110
and it's only on the wide
angle on the iPhone 11.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:43.943
The sun just went down.

00:07:43.943 --> 00:07:46.480
It's not really dark enough
to really show you guys

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.590
how incredible Night Mode...

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:49.503
You are going to shut up.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.583
You're going to shut your mouth now.

00:07:52.583 --> 00:07:53.920
(laughing)

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.080
Obviously Night Mode
hand held is pretty good

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.420
but the tripod Night Mode
is where this really shines.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.910
Let's go find some darkness.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.888
Not that I don't love the
industrial roof or anything.

00:08:04.888 --> 00:08:07.471
(upbeat music)

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:19.700
- Oh God!

00:08:19.986 --> 00:08:23.403
(upbeat music continues)

00:08:30.552 --> 00:08:33.969
(upbeat music continues)

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:40.930
- I'm so scared.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.460
I'm not gonna sleep tonight.

00:08:45.381 --> 00:08:47.964
(upbeat music)

00:08:48.996 --> 00:08:50.740
- It's creepy!

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:53.373
I'm never gonna be able
to sleep, ever again.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.053
That's a lie,

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.400
but it is really spooky.

00:08:58.606 --> 00:09:01.189
(upbeat music)

00:09:14.346 --> 00:09:17.763
(upbeat music continues)

00:09:23.536 --> 00:09:26.619
- [Justine] I can't wait to see this.

00:09:27.522 --> 00:09:29.855
Wow! Look at the difference.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.170
You could actually see the clouds moving

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:36.370
because it was able to take a 30 sec shot

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:37.780
Wow!

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.290
Well, I think you guys get the point.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:44.660
Ultra Wide Night Mode on
the iPhone 12 is incredible.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.670
Alright, I'm hungry.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:47.321
We're done with this video now.

00:09:47.321 --> 00:09:48.982
(laughing)

00:09:48.982 --> 00:09:52.232
(plane engine roaring)

